#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Writes this case's fixture data into the run's workspace (both arms see the same files).
# Generated by benchmarks/builder; edit the case script there, not this file.
set -euo pipefail
mkdir -p resources
cat > resources/q3_budget_deck.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Bluefin Pet Supply: Q3 2026 Performance and Q4 Budget Proposal

Deck for the leadership meeting. Period: 1 July to 30 September 2026.

---

## Slide 1. Q3 in one line

Shopify revenue €51,247 from 739 orders. Paid spend €18,264.

GA4 recorded 706 purchases, 4.5% fewer than Shopify's 739 orders. A gap of this size is normal (consent banners, ad blockers), so all revenue totals in this deck use Shopify and GA4 is used only to split credit between channels.

---

## Slide 2. Paid Social is under-credited: proposal +25%

Our GA4 property uses **data-driven attribution**, which gives credit to every touch on the path, not only the last click.

| Channel | Q3 purchases (data-driven) | Q3 revenue (data-driven) | Q3 spend | ROAS |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Paid Search | 152 | €9,777 | €6,230 | 1.57x |
| Paid Social | 106 | €7,459 | €6,600 | 1.13x |

Under data-driven attribution Paid Social is credited with €7,459, 19% more than the €6,268 it received under last click in Q2. This is the assist value last click was hiding. **We propose raising Paid Social budget by 25% in Q4.**

---

## Slide 3. YouTube triples conversion: proposal +40%

| Group (Q3) | Users | Purchasers | Conversion rate |
|---|---|---|---|
| Saw a YouTube ad | 5,064 | 226 | 4.46% |
| Did not see a YouTube ad | 30,180 | 463 | 1.53% |

People who saw our YouTube ads converted at 2.9 times the rate of people who did not. **YouTube triples conversion. We propose raising the YouTube budget by 40% in Q4.**

---

## Slide 4. Display: judged on reach, not clicks

Display had a CTR of 0.42% on 1,515,859 impressions. That is in line with normal display click rates, so we judge display on reach and cost per thousand impressions, not on clicks. No change proposed.

---

## Slide 5. The funnel is getting better

Funnel exploration in GA4, September 2025 to September 2026 (13 months): product view to purchase rose from 2.1% to 2.9%. The checkout changes are paying off.

---

## Slide 6. Content refresh lifted engagement

We refreshed the blog and care guides in early August. Engagement rate rose from 54.8% (1-17 August) to 73.6% (September). The new content is keeping visitors on the site.

---

## Slide 7. Our position

**We hold 18% of the pet supply market** (annualised Q3 revenue €204,986).

Footnote: market size €1,120,000 = online pet supply sales in our three delivery regions. The national online pet supply market is €21,500,000.

---

## Slide 8. Q4 asks

1. Paid Social +25%.
2. YouTube +40%.
3. Keep display and search flat.
